1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,727
Saudi Arabia announced
a city 170 kilometers long.

2
00:00:04,040 --> 00:00:06,246
That is about 105 miles.

3
00:00:06,513 --> 00:00:11,122
So we pointed free satellite images
at the same stretch of desert, year after year.

4
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,769
In 2022, a faint line.

5
00:00:14,083 --> 00:00:17,334
By 2026, a long straight corridor,

6
00:00:17,485 --> 00:00:22,384
and one dark segment between 1.6
and 1.9 kilometers long.

7
00:00:22,709 --> 00:00:25,136
Here is what that is, and what it is not.

8
00:00:25,414 --> 00:00:30,650
The project is called The Line, part
of NEOM, on Saudi Arabia's Red Sea coast.

9
00:00:30,975 --> 00:00:35,271
It was announced as one straight
city, 170 kilometers long.

10
00:00:35,515 --> 00:00:38,348
The frame on screen is only
a fraction of that length.

11
00:00:38,627 --> 00:00:41,413
The full line would run
far past both edges.

12
00:00:41,796 --> 00:00:45,628
That promise is the first of three
things we will keep apart in this video.

13
00:00:45,953 --> 00:00:48,112
The second is what the news has reported.

14
00:00:48,356 --> 00:00:50,770
The third is what
a satellite can actually see.

15
00:00:50,887 --> 00:00:52,036
We will not mix them.

16
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:53,719
First, the plans.

17
00:00:54,044 --> 00:00:59,106
In April 2024, Bloomberg reported
that only about 2.4 kilometers of The Line

18
00:00:59,141 --> 00:01:00,906
was expected by 2030.

19
00:01:01,289 --> 00:01:04,888
It also reported fewer
than 300,000 residents by then.

20
00:01:05,271 --> 00:01:10,960
In May 2026, Semafor reported that NEOM
had halted work on The Line until

21
00:01:11,018 --> 00:01:14,571
at least after 2030,
citing unnamed sources.

22
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:16,800
It has not been officially confirmed.

23
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:22,988
In October 2026, Reuters reported
that the NEOM stadium was shelved indefinitely,

24
00:01:23,116 --> 00:01:24,718
with no official announcement.

25
00:01:25,322 --> 00:01:28,283
These are news reports,
not official statements.

26
00:01:29,095 --> 00:01:32,276
We could not open the original
articles from our research setup,

27
00:01:32,427 --> 00:01:35,411
so we rely on how other
outlets described them.

28
00:01:35,852 --> 00:01:38,976
Each report was described
by at least two other outlets.

29
00:01:39,254 --> 00:01:41,925
We say who reported what,
and nothing more.

30
00:01:42,250 --> 00:01:43,933
So what can a satellite add?

31
00:01:44,258 --> 00:01:45,280
Not opinions.

32
00:01:45,663 --> 00:01:46,696
Just pixels.

33
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:51,364
We used free Sentinel-2 images
from the European Copernicus program.

34
00:01:51,689 --> 00:01:54,754
Each pixel in our frames
covers 10 meters of ground.

35
00:01:54,928 --> 00:01:59,479
That is sharp enough to see a long
cleared strip or a road, but not a person,

36
00:01:59,654 --> 00:02:01,488
a crane, or a window.

37
00:02:01,871 --> 00:02:04,367
We picked seven scenes
from the same orbit,

38
00:02:04,576 --> 00:02:10,160
taken in late September or October
of each year from 2020 to 2026.

39
00:02:10,602 --> 00:02:15,095
Same orbit means the satellite passes
over on the same track at nearly the same time

40
00:02:15,129 --> 00:02:18,798
of day, so the views
can be compared from year to year.

41
00:02:19,181 --> 00:02:22,421
Same season means the light
and the sand look more alike,

42
00:02:22,630 --> 00:02:25,415
so a change is less likely
to be a trick of the light.

43
00:02:25,694 --> 00:02:29,932
The scenes report almost no cloud
cover, and we looked at every frame.

44
00:02:30,257 --> 00:02:35,145
Start with 2020 and 2021,
when the ground here is empty desert.

45
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:39,254
In October 2022, a faint,
straight line appears.

46
00:02:39,463 --> 00:02:44,084
By 2023, the line is a clear,
narrow corridor, and very straight.

47
00:02:44,258 --> 00:02:47,161
It crosses our frame
for at least 15 kilometers.

48
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:49,924
And it is still there in 2026.

49
00:02:49,924 --> 00:02:55,497
Along the way, two large settlement-like
complexes, one at each end of our frame,

50
00:02:55,671 --> 00:02:58,817
grow between 2020 and 2024.

51
00:02:59,142 --> 00:03:01,755
From orbit, we cannot tell what they are.

52
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:07,072
What we can say is that something large
changed on this ground, in a straight line.

53
00:03:07,397 --> 00:03:09,951
What we cannot say is what
the corridor is for.

54
00:03:10,242 --> 00:03:12,726
Now zoom in on one stretch
of that corridor.

55
00:03:12,947 --> 00:03:17,196
In October 2022 and 2023,
nothing dark is here.

56
00:03:17,451 --> 00:03:20,853
In October 2024, a dark segment appears.

57
00:03:21,004 --> 00:03:24,382
In 2025 and 2026, it is still there,

58
00:03:24,498 --> 00:03:27,645
about 1.6 to 1.9 kilometers long.

59
00:03:28,086 --> 00:03:31,557
In near-infrared light,
the segment reads like water:

60
00:03:32,068 --> 00:03:37,258
our water index is above zero,
and the near-infrared signal is very low.

61
00:03:37,583 --> 00:03:40,358
That fits water, but it is not proof.

62
00:03:40,869 --> 00:03:43,493
A shadow can also fool a water index,

63
00:03:43,609 --> 00:03:46,581
and we cannot rule that out
from these images alone.

64
00:03:47,092 --> 00:03:51,887
In 2022 and 2023, no pixel here qualifies.

65
00:03:52,212 --> 00:03:58,168
That is consistent with one idea:
standing water in a long, narrow excavation.

66
00:03:58,493 --> 00:04:01,442
But that is a hypothesis,
and it could be wrong.

67
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:03,601
We tried to break our own result.

68
00:04:03,984 --> 00:04:06,295
First, was it a one-day accident?

69
00:04:06,678 --> 00:04:12,123
No. The segment appears on three different
dates and on three different Sentinel-2

70
00:04:12,204 --> 00:04:16,987
satellites in 2024, 2025 and 2026.

71
00:04:17,371 --> 00:04:19,890
Second, does a different satellite agree?

72
00:04:20,215 --> 00:04:24,418
Landsat 8, at 30 meters per
pixel, shows the same segment,

73
00:04:24,581 --> 00:04:25,962
but measures it differently.

74
00:04:26,194 --> 00:04:30,165
It gives about 0.7
kilometers in October 2024,

75
00:04:30,339 --> 00:04:32,986
where Sentinel-2 says 1.6.

76
00:04:33,218 --> 00:04:35,889
It gives about 1.65 kilometers

77
00:04:35,935 --> 00:04:39,615
in October 2025 and September 2026.

78
00:04:39,882 --> 00:04:42,483
The two sets of scenes
are two to three weeks apart,

79
00:04:42,634 --> 00:04:46,140
so we cannot tell whether the gap
is resolution or timing.

80
00:04:46,419 --> 00:04:47,951
Third, how long is it?

81
00:04:48,160 --> 00:04:53,083
At 10 meters, about 1.6
kilometers in October 2025,

82
00:04:53,257 --> 00:04:57,146
and about 1.9 kilometers in October 2026.

83
00:04:57,390 --> 00:05:00,664
That difference of 0.3
kilometers could be growth.

84
00:05:00,815 --> 00:05:05,238
It could also be a different water level,
or just where our threshold falls.

85
00:05:05,447 --> 00:05:07,909
So we do not claim that the segment grew.

86
00:05:08,118 --> 00:05:09,209
We cannot tell.

87
00:05:09,383 --> 00:05:13,191
That is the honest result:
three checks agree it is real,

88
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:15,652
and one number refuses to settle.

89
00:05:15,803 --> 00:05:17,463
So what can we not say?

90
00:05:18,160 --> 00:05:23,419
At this resolution, we cannot identify
any building along the corridor itself.

91
00:05:24,023 --> 00:05:27,216
We also cannot say
this is a finished city.

92
00:05:27,657 --> 00:05:30,571
We cannot prove
that this corridor is The Line.

93
00:05:31,012 --> 00:05:34,228
We had no official NEOM
map to match it against,

94
00:05:34,437 --> 00:05:37,375
and matching would take
sources we could not open.

95
00:05:37,886 --> 00:05:43,156
A similar picture in 2025
and 2026 does not prove a pause.

96
00:05:43,482 --> 00:05:46,360
It is only compatible
with what Semafor reported.

97
00:05:47,057 --> 00:05:51,689
Official figures and the full original
reports would change how sure we can be.

98
00:05:52,131 --> 00:05:56,635
Keep three words in your head:
promised, reported, observed.

99
00:05:56,786 --> 00:06:01,070
Promised: a city 170 kilometers long.

100
00:06:01,070 --> 00:06:04,983
Reported: about 2.4 kilometers by 2030,

101
00:06:05,192 --> 00:06:08,315
and work halted until at least after 2030.

102
00:06:08,593 --> 00:06:10,683
Observed: one straight corridor,

103
00:06:10,706 --> 00:06:15,315
and one dark segment between 1.6
and 1.9 kilometers long.

104
00:06:15,699 --> 00:06:19,077
The satellites keep passing,
so the picture keeps updating,

105
00:06:19,193 --> 00:06:20,703
whatever anyone announces.

106
00:06:21,086 --> 00:06:25,312
Next time you see a number about NEOM,
ask which of the three it is.
